<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">Warsaw Pact invasion of Czechoslovakia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1968</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw-pact">Warsaw Pact</a> invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> began on the night of 20–21 August 1968, when troops of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> entered the country to end <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-dubcek">Alexander Dubček</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague-spring">Prague Spring</a> reforms. Resistance was largely non-violent, but more than a hundred civilians were killed. Soviet troops remained in Czechoslovakia until 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/warsaw-pact-invasion-of-czechoslovakia.jpg" alt="Warsaw Pact invasion of Czechoslovakia" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Главцентроархив · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Invasion_of_Czechoslovakia_collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
